# Every text file keeps LF on every checkout, Windows runners included (their
# git sets core.autocrlf=true): sources, scripts, expected compiler output
# (tools/tests/ispeak_test.sh, the runner's خرج-تشخيص headers) and fixtures
# are read byte for byte, as the compiler writes and reads them on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows PowerShell scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Binary: never converted, even when the bytes look like text (an archive
# that is only `!<arch>\n`, a #embed resource, the compressed seed).
*.a   binary
*.bin binary
*.zst binary
